-artificial-intelligence-bias">What is Artificial Intelligence Bias</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/who-is-the-father-of-artificial-intelligence">Who is the Father of Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/sop-for-ms-in-artificial-intelligence">SOP for MS in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/top-ai-penny-stocks-in-india">Top AI Penny Stocks in India</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/what-is-ai-in-data-analytics">What is AI in Data Analytics</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/artificial-intelligence-in-business-management">Artificial Intelligence in Business Management</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/partial-order-planning-in-artificial-intelligence">Partial Order Planning in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/artificial-intelligence-in-auditing">Artificial Intelligence in Auditing</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/artificial-intelligence-in-construction">Artificial Intelligence in Construction</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/information-retrieval-in-artificial-intelligence">Information Retrieval in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/artificial-intelligence-in-psychology">Artificial Intelligence in Psychology</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/iterative-deepening-search-in-artificial-intelligence">Iterative Deepening Search in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/applications-of-deep-learning-in-artificial-intelligence">Applications of Deep Learning in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/7-artificial-intelligence-projects-in-agriculture">7 Artificial Intelligence Projects in Agriculture</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/what-is-multimodal-ai">What is Multimodal AI</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/benefits-of-artificial-intelligence-in-business">Benefits of Artificial Intelligence in Business</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/conceptual-graphs-in-artificial-intelligence">Conceptual Graphs in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/problem-space-and-search-in-artificial-intelligence">Problem Space and Search in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/conditional-planning-in-artificial-intelligence">Conditional Planning in Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/informed-search-algorithms-in-artificial-intelligence">Informed Search Algorithms in Artificial Intelligence</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item" style="background-color:var(--sidebar)"><h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading10"><button aria-controls="flush-collapse10" aria-expanded="true" class="accordion-button sidebar-btn" data-bs-target="#flush-collapse10" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">Related Tutorials</button></h2><div aria-labelledby="flush-heading10" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" id="flush-collapse10"><div class="accordion-body"><ul><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/tensorflow">Tensorflow Tutorial</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/pytorch">PyTorch Tutorial</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/reinforcement-learning">Reinforcement Learning</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-12 col-md-7"><div class="overview"><html><head></head><body><div id="city"><table><tbody><tr><td><div id="bottomnextup"><a class="next" href="the-role-of-artificial-intelligence-in-waste-management">next →</a> <a class="next" href="role-of-ai-in-the-mortgage-industry">← prev</a></div><h1 class="h1">Role of Artificial Intelligence in Modern Society</h1><div style="font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:#6f6e6e"><span>17 Apr 2025</span> | <span><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 14 min read</span></div><h2 class="h2">Introduction</h2><p>AI has taken the society and is possibly intersecting all facets of society in equal measure. Ranking from medication to transportation, smart AI systems are helping to perform their tasks more precisely, many times offering a level of customization. Diagnosis of diseases is made easier by AI because it can work on images and analysis of patterns to give forecasts, hence enhancing the outcomes of the patients. In the transportation industry, Artificial Intelligence is implemented where the implementation of self-driving vehicles, as well as improved traffic patterns, creates safer roads with limited traffic jams. In addition, Entertainment and e-commerce industries use recommendation systems licensed through machine intelligence to give every customer a unique experience based on their preferences.</p><h2 class="h2">AI in Communication and Social Connectivity</h2><h3 class="h3">Enhanced Customer Support</h3><p><a href="artificial-intelligence-ai">AI</a> is changing customer support solutions such as chatbots and <a href="ai-virtual-assistant-using-python">virtual assistants</a>. Such systems have prompt replies, meaning that customer queries can be answered at any time of the day. Present-day computerized AI chatbots using <a href="what-is-natural-language-processing-in-artificial-intelligence">NLP</a> are in a position to address intricate requests with similar inflexion and tenor or diction. These enable organizations to provide optimized response time and cut down operational costs, hence improving the user experience.</p><h3 class="h3">AI-Powered Translation Tools</h3><p>Whether it is in self-generated conversations or written form, language has been able to be dealt with by tools such as Google Translate or DeepL. These are. Machine tools that provide <a href="machine-learning">machine learning</a> services to enable real-time translation of texts or speeches to different languages to foster mutual understanding. They are of huge value to businesses, educators, and travelers, bringing people of the world closer together. In addition, the growth of AI technology means that translated texts are translated taking into account the contextual interpretations and thus improving face cultural translation.</p><h3 class="h3">Social Media Personalization</h3><p>Users interact with social networks and based on that data, AI algorithms provide them relevant information. By using likes, shares and interactions, AI selects preferred material it recommends posts, friends, or groups. While it enhances user interaction through personalization, it creates other problems, such as echo chambers and fake news. The responsibilities of platforms such as Instagram and Facebook are highly dependent on AI to provoke user interaction.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Content Moderation</h3><p>AI is significant when it comes to filtering the content of communication media. Machine learning technology searches through text, images and moving pictures for violating or damaging depictions. In this way, the AI provides safe online communication due to the identification or elimination of unwanted material. Many of the platforms, such as <a href="what-is-youtube">YouTube</a> and twitter, integrate Artificial Intelligence moderation techniques in a way to address the huge traffic of content generated by its users. However, it is still a problem what a publisher is allowed to publish and what should be banned from the publication.</p><h3 class="h3">Virtual Meeting Assistance</h3><p>AI makes virtual meetings richer with such features as transcription and formatting of a meeting, as well as translation. Techniques such as <a href="zoom-alternatives">Zoom</a> and <a href="microsoft-company">Microsoft</a> Teams include artificial intelligence to enhance communication effectiveness and thus promote globalization. A good example is the transcription products and services, which support meeting minutes and are enabled by Artificial Intelligence to give accuracy to the affair, which in turn works to free participants from having to take down the events one by one. These features refer mainly to integrating with remote or hybrid working schemes because they help eliminate communication breakdowns in remote teams.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Healthcare</h2><h3 class="h3">Medical Imaging and Diagnostics</h3><p>Medical imaging for AI has gone from accelerating diagnostic accuracy dramatically to enabling faster and more efficient data collection. Simple things like X-rays, <a href="mri-full-form">MRI</a> or <a href="ct-scan-full-form">CT scans</a> will feel like AI-powered algorithms that will act like detectors for tumours, fractures, or cardiovascular issues. It allows fast and better identification of abnormalities in contrast to standard methods and early intervention and treatment. Clearly, they can't just be doctors other tools like Google's Deepmind system, an AI used to diagnose a host of different cancers and eye diseases, have had remarkable success. It reduces workload of the radiologist and provides better outcomes for patients.</p><h3 class="h3">Drug Discovery and Development</h3><p>Accelerated drug discovery is done by using a huge dataset and analyzing the dataset using AI. Machine learning models are used to simulate molecular interactions and drug efficacy to be predicted and reduce the need for extensive trial and error experiments. Companies like Moderna say AI significantly reduced the time it would have taken to develop the <a href="covid-19-full-form">COVID-19</a> vaccine from 10 years to five. With its help, the time and money necessary to get new treatments to market are reduced in healthcare around the world.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Personalized Medicine</h3><p>It further means that AI can provide the delivery of personalized healthcare for analyzing patient data, genetics and lifestyle. This can be used to develop a tailored therapy and predict a patient's response to therapies. For instance, IBM Watson Health deploys AI to suggest how to address a unique case of cancer for that specific person. Better treatment outcomes and fewer adverse side effects mean better quality of care.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Surgery</h3><p>AI-powered robotic surgical system (da Vinci Surgical System) is a robotic surgical system that facilitates clinical operations during minimally invasive procedures. Improvements in these systems are an increase in precision, from no surgical error to no recovery period. And even surgical videos are fed into AI which then recommends improvements and perfected techniques. By integrating AI, other people achieve better patient safety and outcomes, especially in complex surgery.</p><h3 class="h3">Remote Patient Monitoring</h3><p>Devices powered by AI, such as the Fitbit or the Apple Watch, all monitor vital signs like heart rate, blood pressure, and blood oxygen level in real time. They capture data from patients and send it to care providers for active management of chronic illnesses like diabetes or hypertension. Then AI analyzes this data looks for anomalies, informs doctors or patients and can assist with timely intervention. It reduces visits to hospitals and improves preventive care.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Education</h2><h3 class="h3">Personalized Learning</h3><p>Being able to personalize learning experiences makes learning more relevant for an individual. AI Data-driven platforms like Khan Academy and Coursera create powerful algorithms to predict the performance of the students, pace, and preferred learning approach to provide tailor-made lessons and suggestions. It also makes sure that students can focus their effort on what they struggle with and move along quickly with the things they are good at. Not only does personal e-learning increase academic outcomes, but it also encourages students to be more engaged and motivated.</p><h3 class="h3">Intelligent Tutoring Systems</h3><p>One example of that is AI-powered tutoring systems from companies like Carnegie Learning and Squirrel AI, which provide one-on-one support to students in a way that emulates the personal tutor experience. The systems adjust to the pace and style of learning of the students from their knowledge gaps and mentor the students along this path, giving them guidance in steps and instant feedback. In math and science especially, problem-solving can be completed with iterative practice, so they are particularly helpful.</p><p><strong>Automated Grading and Feedback</strong></p><p>Grading assignments, quizzes, or exams can be automated with AI, making the process really simple. Gradescope is just one of the tools out there that use machine learning to assess answers, spot trends, and provide rich feedback to the students. It improves the workload for educators to leave them to teach instead of focusing on administrative work.</p><h3 class="h3">Virtual Classrooms and AI-Powered Learning Platforms</h3><p>AI makes it possible to have virtual classrooms that offer an immersive and interactive learning environment. AI is being used in practice by platforms like Google Classroom and Microsoft Teams to provide real-time language translation, speech-to-text features, and teaching analytics about how much their students participate in their courses. Through these innovations, education, on average, becomes more accessible, especially in remote or underserved areas. AI-powered tools also help teachers keep an eye on the progress of the students and accordingly teach.</p><h3 class="h3">Language Learning and Translation</h3><p>An incredible number of language learning tools have seen their evolution thanks to artificial intelligence, in the form of Duolingo or Babbel, which uses natural language processing to teach vocabulary, grammar, and pronunciation. The advances of AI on these platforms are that they use AI to track learner progress and adjust the lessons dynamically. Moreover, AI-based translation tools, such as Google Translate, have addressed the problem of languages, which has broken the language barrier for students to gain access to educational materials in their languages.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Entertainment</h2><h3 class="h3">Content Recommendation Systems</h3><p>Recommendation systems on platforms such as <a href="netflix-alternatives">Netflix</a>, Spotify, and even YouTube are powered by AI, which uses user preferences, viewing habits, and engagement to recommend what they think you'd like. This personalizes content for the user, keeping the user interested in what they see in tailored movies, shows, or songs. They make the user experience better by reducing the time to search and, increasing content discovery, increasing platform retention. Netflix's AI forecasts what particular users would like to watch based on history and all over the world's trends.</p><h3 class="h3">AI-Generated Music and Art</h3><p>The entertainment world is being transformed by AI which makes music, art, and design. Platforms like DeepArt bring AI-generated visual art, and OpenAI's MuseNet and Amper Music provide tools for composing computerized melodies, as Chad Bocon, a three-year Digital Design and Rhetoric student in the IFDRA, stated. These innovations allow creators to experiment with new ideas and reduce production costs. For example, AI-produced compositions are used in video games, advertising, and independent films to produce diverse creative outputs.</p><h3 class="h3">Special Effects and CGI in Movies</h3><p>But CGI special effects are at the heart of AI and depend crucially on it. NVIDIA's AI-based rendering AI tools reduce production time by enhancing visual effects. The technology of deepfake is also applied for the creation of lifelike characters, voice dubbing and scene enhancement. Not only does it boost visual storytelling in CGI, but it also makes those laborious related processes in traditional CGI redundant.</p><h3 class="h3">Video Game Development and NPC Behavior</h3><p>Using AI, we've been able to increase non-playable characters (NPCs) and game design. To make NPC more smart and reflective, AI algorithms are used to introduce dynamic interaction, which will responsively react to player behavior. Further, AI is used to generate game environments and test gameplay by AI. AI-powered NPCs in games such as The Last of Us Part II create a more realistic immersive experience for the player.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Scriptwriting and Storytelling</h3><p>More and more, artificial intelligence is being used to help in scriptwriting and storytelling. ScriptBook analyzes scripts for sales potential and predicts audience interest on platforms such as itself. AI plot ideas, dialogues, and even character arcs are all generated for the screenwriter, freeing him to get out of an authorial block.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Jobs</h2><h3 class="h3">Automating Repetitive Tasks</h3><p>Automation has forced businesses to innovate by automating repetitive tasks such as data entry, scheduling customer inquiries, and many more. Robotic Process Automation (RPA) tools facilitate these processes, freeing up employees time to do more creative, strategic, or complicated work. For example, AI-powered chatbots in customer service handle routine queries, reducing human workload. But in industries such as banking and insurance also, reduced operational costs and precision in common day-to-day tasks are of huge benefit.</p><h3 class="h3">Job Creation in AI Development and Maintenance</h3><p>AI automates some roles but creates jobs for developing, managing, and maintaining this technology. They're hiring people in high-demand roles like AI engineers, data scientists, and machine learning specialists. These people create, test, and optimize AI systems operating in different industries. In addition, there are jobs in AI ethics and governance that will keep AI systems responsible and thereby help us advance more smoothly. There is a lot of hiring going on here from companies like Google and IBM.</p><h3 class="h3">Upskilling and Reskilling the Workforce</h3><p>Reskilling and upskilling workers are entirely driven by the need to adapt workers to changing job demands via AI. In order to support employees with digital and AI-related skills such as coding, data analysis, and AI system management, many companies spend money on training programs. For example, Amazon's 'Upskilling 2025' program trains employees in tech-based roles to equip them for AI-enabled job markets.</p><h3 class="h3">Enhancing Recruitment Processes</h3><p>AI manipulates recruiting procedures by naturally screening applicants and matching skills to activity necessities, as of now diminishing bias in providing choices. LinkedIn Talent Solutions and HireVue leverage AI-powered tools that analyze resumes conduct video interviews, and project candidate success.</p><h3 class="h3">AI-Powered Decision Support Systems</h3><p>AI assists managers and employees in decision-making through advanced analytics and predictive models. AI tools allow teams to apply business data to see insights such as what to market, how to run a supply chain, or how they should manage projects. As an example, AI-based tools like <a href="tableau">Tableau</a> and <a href="power-bi">Power BI</a> make <a href="what-is-data-visualization">data visualization</a> simpler so that businesses can quickly make strategic decisions.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Transportation</h2><h3 class="h3">Autonomous Vehicles</h3><p>Autonomous vehicles use AI as their foundation to confidently move on a road. The data from such sensors as cameras, LiDAR, and radar drive machine-learning algorithms to detect obstacles, predict traffic patterns, and make real-time decisions. Compared to these companies, all other car makers in the world have done very little to develop autonomous cars and trucks, even though this would certainly help to decrease the frequency of accidents resulting from human error and, at the very least, make transportation more efficient. There are other tests of autonomous vehicles as well, in public transportation systems so that people can experience some element of the future of urban mobility.</p><h3 class="h3">Predictive Maintenance for Fleet Management</h3><p>Whenever vehicles are in service, they are predicted to have some maintenance needs. Wear and tear is detected in these predictive maintenance systems by analyzing sensor data so that shutdowns do not occur due to unexpected breakdowns and so that downtime can be eliminated. Logistics companies like FedEx and DHL are using the AI-based fleet management system for monitoring vehicles' health, so the cars get repaired within a timely manner as well as saving cost. This approach improves reliability and prolongs vehicle life to increase the efficiency of transportation and logistics operations.</p><h3 class="h3">Traffic Management and Optimization</h3><p>With real time traffic monitoring and predictive analytics, AI helps solve traffic flow issues and reduce congestion of traffic. Traffic cameras, <a href="global-positioning-systems">GPS</a>, and sensor data are analyzed by AI-powered systems that optimize traffic signals, reprogram cars, and cut down on travel times. Projects like smart cities in Singapore as well as Amsterdam are using AI to manage urban transportation networks to have less delay and reduce fuel consumption.</p><h3 class="h3">Enhancing Public Transportation Systems</h3><p>AI can help optimize how and where public transportation runs, when it runs, and how the passengers of those transportation experiences. The dynamic services feature is based on the fact that AI systems study how commercial passenger demand, travel patterns, and weather conditions change over time. The Delhi Metro uses AI to manage train schedules and load not just more people on those trains but to do so with maximum efficiency.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Aviation</h3><p>Like any other major industry, aviation is being touched by AI in flight operations, maintenance, and passenger experience. Airlines also save in fuel savings from route optimization, fuel efficiency, aircraft predictive maintenance, etc. AI. The check-in, boarding, and customer inquiries are handled with facts recognition, and AI chatbots address the queries. Delta Airlines uses AI to improve operational efficiency in terms of improving customer experience with resulting cost savings in operations.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in MNC</h2><h3 class="h3">Enhanced Decision-Making</h3><p>Artificial intelligence helps multinational companies make decisions by processing data inputs. AI systems examine big data collections for trends and threats that help executive leaders make strategic choices with the knowledge they need. Google depends on AI technology to strengthen operational approaches and spot market direction patterns. Through these insights, MNCs maintain their market position and adaptation speed in continuously changing global business environments.</p><h3 class="h3">AI in Marketing Campaigns</h3><p>Combined with AI, MNCs can launch precise marketing initiatives through systems that segment markets based on consumer behavior analysis. With AI, Coca-Cola monitors customer emotions to generate marketing strategies that suit particular market segments. Through AI-powered predictive analysis, organizations can present customer-specific ads, which drive conversion rates up and strengthen brand-user ties.</p><h3 class="h3">Improved Workplace Productivity</h3><p>Companies that operate globally increase their workplace effectiveness through artificial intelligence tools that automate tasks and enhance teamwork. Microsoft implements numerical applications such as AI throughout Office 365 to minimize workloads with automated tasks, including document processing and content transformation. Artificial intelligence systems deliver insights to workers enabling them to distribute tasks accordingly and optimize management of time. These tools drive innovation while delivering decreased workload burdens and allowing teams to dedicate themselves to significant work activities.</p><h3 class="h3">Personalized Customer Experiences</h3><p>Organizations use AI to provide customized customer interactions by deploying smart chatbots together with recommendation software. Through AI algorithms, Amazon, together with Netflix, studies how users act and what they prefer to deliver personalized suggestions for products or content. The artificial intelligence behind virtual assistants Siri and Alexa gives customers instant assistance during their interactions. The implementation of these applications delivers worldwide positive effects on customer satisfaction alongside heightened loyalty.</p><h2 class="h2">Artificial Intelligence in Smart Cities</h2><h3 class="h3">Traffic Management and Optimization</h3><p>In smart cities, AI does traffic flow management and optimization from real-time sensors, cameras and GPS data. It can predict traffic congestion, adjust traffic signals so as to reduce delays in congested regions, and thereby improve total urban mobility. Cities like Singapore and Los Angeles use AI to dynamically change traffic patterns depending on real conditions, keeping commutes smoother, travel times shorter, and emissions lower.</p><h3 class="h3">Waste Management Systems</h3><p>AI-powered smart waste management systems are revolutionizing our urban environments. Predicting waste levels and recommendations on schedule will enable the optimization of waste collection to minimize cost and improve the overall operational efficiency utilizing the aid of AI. Seoul is one area that uses AI-driven systems to monitor waste bins to see when they are full so there are no more unnecessary trips. As this technology can also be used in recycling processes, it automatically identifies recyclable materials.</p><h3 class="h3">Energy Consumption and Grid Management</h3><p>Smart cities AI provides electrical optimization optimizing energy consumption by monitoring and analyzing its usage in real time. Smart grids powered by AI-driven machine learning algorithms adjust energy distribution to avert future consumption and drive both power use efficiency and waste. New York is using AI to balance energy loads and integrate renewable energy sources into a balance better than it does for sustainability.</p><h3 class="h3">Public Safety and Surveillance</h3><p>Real-time AI-powered surveillance systems help smart cities prevent them from getting themselves into potential threats or criminal activities. Public cameras are fed with data, and advanced computer vision systems analyze this data to detect abnormal behaviour AI-driven algorithms predict and prevent crimes, using patterns to detect future atrocity. The AI is helping law enforcement teams not to react but to prevent these incidents proactively.</p><h3 class="h3">Urban Planning and Development</h3><p>Urban planning leverages large lists of population growth, traffic, environmental conditions, and infrastructure to analyze and aid decision-making through the use of AI. These insights help city planners build better, more efficient, and more sustainable urban environments. AI algorithms are used to predict what future urban development needs are and which decisions to make about land use and infrastructure investments. Toronto lives among cities that are using AI to design smarter urban layouts that allow cities to grow without wrecking the environmental and human sphere.</p><h2 class="h2">Conclusion</h2><p>In modern society, Artificial Intelligence has a transformative role, from the standard of healthcare through education to transportation and communication. It makes it more efficient and more innovative and helps make decisions faster through real time analysis of enormous amounts of data. Integration of AI in industries such as manufacturing, healthcare, and smart cities has enabled automation, personalization, and sustainability. enhanced quality of life), these need to be balanced with ethical concerns and job displacement.</p><hr/><div class="nexttopicdiv"><span class="nexttopictext">Next Topic</span><span class="nexttopiclink"><a href="the-role-of-artificial-intelligence-in-waste-management">The-role-of-artificial-intelligence-in-waste-management</a></span></div><br/><br/><div id="bottomnext"><a class="next" href="role-of-ai-in-the-mortgage-industry" style="float:left">← prev</a> <a class="next" href="the-role-of-artificial-intelligence-in-waste-management" style="float:right">next →</a></div><br/><br/></td></tr></tbody></table></div></body></html><br/></div><div class="related-posts-container"><h2 class="h3">Related Posts</h2><ul class="related-posts-list"><li><a class="related-post-item" href="jarvis-artificial-intelligence-software"><h3 class="h3">Jarvis Artificial Intelligence Software</h3><p class="related-post-content">Introduction Machine learning, a subset of artificial intelligence (AI), has rapidly developed, improving all aspects of life in diverse fields. In particular, one of the most famous types of AI interface or system recognized in the popular media and even in articles and other material is "Jarvis"...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 7 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="genetic-algorithm-in-soft-computing"><h3 class="h3">Genetic Algorithm in Soft Computing</h3><p class="related-post-content">A genetic algorithm (GA), which is a subset of the larger class of evolutionary algorithms (EA), is a metaheuristic used in computer science and 